{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nTask SE-PE-01: Grammar-guided node reduction (Perses-style syntax-guided reduction)\n\nThe rules are:\n1. Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes (process deepest first)\n2. Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\n3. Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\n4. Use node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth\n5. Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order\n\nLet me trace through the first example to understand the algorithm:\n\nCase 000:\nNodes:\n- root: depth 0, symbol \"root\", removable=false\n- n1: depth 1, symbol \"s1\", removable=false\n- n2: depth 1, symbol \"s2\", removable=true\n- n3: depth 1, symbol \"s0\", removable=false\n- n4: depth 2, symbol \"s1\", removable=true, parent=n2\n- n5: depth 2, symbol \"s2\", removable=false, parent=n3\n- n6: depth 2, symbol \"s0\", removable=true, parent=n1\n\nRequired symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nProcessing order: deepest first, then by node ID as tie-break.\n\nDepth 2 nodes (sorted by ID): n4, n5, n6\nDepth 1 nodes (sorted by ID): n1, n2, n3\nDepth 0 nodes: root\n\nProcess n4 (depth 2, symbol \"s1\", removable=true, parent=n2):\n- Check: can we remove n4?\n- n4 has no children (nothing has parent=n4), so no retained children issue\n- If we remove n4, which symbols remain? root (root), s1 (n1), s2 (n2, n5), s0 (n3, n6)\n- Required symbols: root -\u003e present (root node), s1 -\u003e still present (n1 has s1)\n- So we CAN remove n4. Remove it.\n\nProcess n5 (depth 2, symbol \"s2\", removable=false):\n- removable=false, so skip (cannot remove)\n\nProcess n6 (depth 2, symbol \"s0\", removable=true, parent=n1):\n- n6 has no children\n- If we remove n6, symbols remaining: root (root), s1 (n1), s2 (n2, n5), s0 (n3)\n- Required: root -\u003e yes, s1 -\u003e yes\n- So we CAN remove n6. Remove it.\n\nNow depth 1 nodes. But wait - n4 was removed. n2's children: n4 was removed, so n2 has no retained children now.\n\nProcess n1 (depth 1, symbol \"s1\", removable=false):\n- removable=false, skip\n\nProcess n2 (depth 1, symbol \"s2\", removable=true, parent=root):\n- n2's children: n4 (already removed). So no retained children.\n- If we remove n2: symbols remaining: root (root), s1 (n1), s0 (n3), s2 (n5)\n- Required: root -\u003e yes, s1 -\u003e yes\n- So we CAN remove n2. Remove it.\n\nProcess n3 (depth 1, symbol \"s0\", removable=false):\n- removable=false, skip\n\nProcess root (depth 0, removable=false):\n- Skip\n\nFinal:\n- Removed: n4, n6, n2 (in removal order)\n- Retained: root, n1, n3, n5 (sorted)\n\nLet me verify case 001 similarly:\n\nRequired symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nDepth 2 nodes (sorted by ID): n4, n5, n6\n\nn4 (depth 2, symbol \"s1\", removable=true, parent=n2):\n- No children of n4\n- If removed: symbols remain: root, s1 (n1), s2 (n2, n5), s0 (n3, n6)\n- Required: root (yes), s1 (yes via n1)\n- Remove n4.\n\nn5 (depth 2, symbol \"s2\", removable=false):\n- Skip\n\nn6 (depth 2, symbol \"s0\", removable=true, parent=n1):\n- No children\n- If removed: symbols: root, s1 (n1), s2 (n2, n5), s0 (n3)\n- Required: root, s1 -\u003e both present\n- Remove n6.\n\nDepth 1:\nn1 (removable=false): skip\nn2 (depth 1, symbol \"s2\", removable=true):\n- Children: n4 was removed, no retained children\n- If removed: symbols: root, s1 (n1), s0 (n3), s2 (n5)\n- Required: yes\n- Remove n2.\n\nn3 (removable=false): skip\n\nroot: skip\n\nRemoved: n4, n6, n2\nRetained: root, n1, n3, n5\n\nSame result as case 000.\n\nCase 002: Same structure, same result likely.\n\nRequired symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nn4 (depth 2, s1, removable=true, parent=n2):\n- If removed: symbols: root, s1 (n1), s2 (n2, n5), s0 (n3, n6)\n- Required present\n- Remove n4.\n\nn5 (removable=false): skip\n\nn6 (depth 2, s0, removable=true, parent=n1):\n- If removed: symbols: root, s1 (n1), s2 (n2, n5), s0 (n3)\n- Required present\n- Remove n6.\n\nDepth 1:\nn1: removable=false, skip\nn2 (s2, removable=true):\n- No retained children (n4 removed)\n- If removed: symbols: root, s1 (n1), s0 (n3), s2 (n5)\n- Required present\n- Remove n2.\n\nn3: removable=false, skip\n\nRemoved: n4, n6, n2\nRetained: root, n1, n3, n5\n\nAll three cases produce the same removal order and retained nodes.\n\nNow let me write the Python implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build lookup structures\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    for n in nodes:\n        for field in (\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"):\n            if field not in n:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Missing field {field} in node {n}\")\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            if n[\"parent\"] not in node_map:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent {n['parent']} not found for node {n['id']}\")\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Track which nodes are currently retained\n    retained = {n[\"id\"] for n in nodes}\n    removal_order = []\n    \n    # Sort nodes: deepest first, then by node ID (lexicographic) as tie-break\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    def get_symbol_coverage(excluded_id):\n        \"\"\"Get set of symbols present if excluded_id is removed.\"\"\"\n        return {node_map[nid][\"symbol\"] for nid in retained if nid != excluded_id}\n    \n    def has_retained_children(node_id):\n        return any(child in retained for child in children[node_id])\n    \n    for n in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = n[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Skip if not removable\n        if not n[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if already removed (shouldn't happen in this pass, but safe)\n        if nid not in retained:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if has retained children\n        if has_retained_children(nid):\n            continue\n        \n        # Check if removing this node preserves all required symbols\n        symbols_after = get_symbol_coverage(nid)\n        if required_symbols.issubset(symbols_after):\n            retained.remove(nid)\n            removal_order.append(nid)\n    \n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removal_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nWait, I need to think about the sorting of retained node IDs. The output schema says \"retained_node_ids\" is an array of strings. The description says \"Return sorted retained IDs\". I'll sort them lexicographically/alphabetically.\n\nLet me also double-check the removal order for the cases:\n- n4, n6, n2 (depth 2 first: n4 then n5(skip) then n6, then depth 1: n1(skip) then n2 then n3(skip))\n\nLooks correct.\n\nNow let me write the final implementation and format as the required JSON envelope.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    required_node_fields = (\\\"id\\\", \\\"parent\\\", \\\"symbol\\\", \\\"depth\\\", \\\"removable\\\", \\\"utility\\\")\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        for field in required_node_fields:\\n            if field not in n:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing field '{field}' in node {n}\\\")\\n\\n    node_map = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n\\n    # Validate parent references\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None and n[\\\"parent\\\"] not in node_map:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Parent '{n['parent']}' not found for node '{n['id']}'\\\")\\n\\n    # Build children map\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            children[n[\\\"parent\\\"]].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    # Track retained nodes\\n    retained = {n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes}\\n    removal_order = []\\n\\n    # Process deepest first; use node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    for n in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = n[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Must be removable\\n        if not n[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Must still be retained\\n        if nid not in retained:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Must have no retained children\\n        if any(child in retained for child in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Check that all required symbols remain after tentative removal\\n        symbols_after = {node_map[rid][\\\"symbol\\\"] for rid in retained if rid != nid}\\n        if not required_symbols.issubset(symbols_after):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Remove the node\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removal_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": sorted(retained)\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_016UeHcUDm96CqB1YFMRXYwu","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2536},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2536,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":54,"output_tokens":2759,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2189},"service_tier":"standard"}}